\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Fill Thou my life, O Lord my God,
\par In every part with praise,
\par That my whole being may proclaim
\par Thy being and Thy ways.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Not for the lips of praise alone,
\par Nor e'en the praising heart,
\par I ask, but for a life made up
\par Of praise in every part:
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Praise in the common things of life,
\par Its going out and in;
\par Praise in each duty and each deed,
\par However small and mean.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Fill every part of me with praise;
\par Let all my being speak
\par Of Thee and of Thy love, O Lord,
\par Poor though I be and weak.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. So shalt Thou, Lord, from me, e'en me,
\par Receive the glory due;
\par And so shall I begin on earth
\par The song for ever new.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. So shall no part of day or night
\par From sacredness be free;
\par But all my life, in every step,
\par Be fellowship with Thee.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

